2.9445127438521013e-05, "top": [["ic", -2.9445127438521013e-05], [" ic", -11.12761402130127]]}, {"t": "px", "lp": -0.0002215750137111172, "top": [["px", -0.0002215750137111172], ["PX", -10.678658485412598]]}, {"t": "`", "lp": -0.0006891479133628309, "top": [["`", -0.0006891479133628309], [" `", -9.956168174743652]]}, {"t": " |", "lp": -0.0003201281651854515, "top": [[" |", -0.0003201281651854515], ["|", -11.103742599487305]]}, {"t": " Use", "lp": -0.0008336203172802925, "top": [[" Use", -0.0008336203172802925], [" Intel", -7.539883613586426]]}, {"t": " Intel", "lp": -0.00030283743399195373, "top": [[" Intel", -0.00030283743399195373], ["Intel", -8.608656883239746]]}, {"t": "'s", "lp": -0.00013698085967916995, "top": [["'s", -0.00013698085967916995], ["\u7684", -10.402414321899414]]}], "text": "# PKGBUILD build() Function: Step-by-Step Explanation\n\nLet me break down this `build()` function line by line.\n\n## The Setup\n\n```bash\nsource /opt/intel/oneapi/setvars.sh --force\n```\nThis loads the Intel oneAPI environment variables (compiler paths, library paths, etc.). The `--force` flag forces the environment to be set up even if it appears already configured. This is essential because we're compiling with Intel's SYCL compilers (`icx`/`icpx`) rather than the default GCC.\n\n```bash\nset -e\n```\nThis makes the script exit immediately if any command returns a non-zero status (an error). It's a safety net so a failed command doesn't leave you with a half-built binary.\n\n## The CMake Configuration\n\nNow the main `cmake` command. Let me flag each part:\n\n| Flag | Meaning |\n|------|---------|\n| `-S \"${srcdir}/llama.cpp\"` | **S**ource directory \u2014 where the source code lives |\n| `-B \"${srcdir}/build\"` | **B**uild directory \u2014 where build artifacts go |\n| `-G Ninja` | Use the **Ninja** build system (fast, efficient) instead of Make |\n| `-DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release` | Optimize for **performance** (adds `-O3`, strips debug info) |\n| `-DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/usr` | Where files will be installed (`/usr`) |\n| `-DCMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDIR=lib` | Libraries go in `/usr/lib` (not `/usr/lib64`) |\n| `-DCMAKE_C_COMPILER=icx` | Use Intel's **C** compiler for C code |\n| `-DCMAKE_CXX_COMPILER=icpx` | Use Intel's"}